"900.4.10(122)": {"explanation": "Exception RS 122 keeps the lot frontage and lot area that existed when By-law 569-2013 was enacted, allows at most two dwelling units per lot on a registered plan, sets side setbacks of 2.4 m (5.7 m next to a street), and requires compliance with exception 900.4.10(336).", "code_refs": "none"},
"900.4.10(176)": {"explanation": "Exception RS 176 allows one semi-detached house per lot, keeps the lot frontage and area that existed when By-law 569-2013 was enacted, sets a 7.5 m setback from a front lot line on Braymore Blvd., side setbacks of 1.2 m (4.5 m next to a street), 40 percent maximum lot coverage, a 0.3 m side setback for an attached garage, parking inside the residential building, and a 6.0 m setback for a garage entrance that faces the street.", "code_refs": "none"},
"900.4.10(51)": {"explanation": "Exception RS 51 allows one semi-detached house per lot, keeps the lot frontage and area that existed when By-law 569-2013 was enacted, and sets side setbacks of 2.4 m (3.6 m next to a street).", "code_refs": "none"}
